id: pm-m4uyyj
title: "GH-1216: Preserve diagnostic identity and sanitize short and bounded error text"
description: Unknown option errors with a long description lose their error title when the 768-token text budget falls back to generic required-option guidance. Preserve the specific error identity and useful corrective action within the SDK budget contract and prove real CLI behavior.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-07T13:35:12.851Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-07T16:38:44.332Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-07T16:38:43.792Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-07T16:38:43.792Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Oversized CLI unknown-option and correction-refusal diagnostics retain the specific flag and corrective action within 768 estimated tokens; minimum 192-token UTF-8 SDK budget remains binding; caller-input echoes are omitted.
goal: project management = context management
value: Reduce diagnostic retries and preserve useful agent context
why_now: New GitHub report exposes an uncovered boundary in required release or agent workflows.
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Sanitize complete diagnostic text before token estimation and preserve safe identity and corrective action in both short and bounded output. Strip terminal escape sequences, replace other control characters, normalize CRLF, and preserve ordinary indentation and line breaks."
expected_result: Short and oversized errors remain identifiable and actionable without terminal-control injection; bounded recovery stays within its declared UTF-8 budget.
actual_result: "Short-output regression first failed, then passed. All 8548 tests passed at exact 100% coverage, including real CLI error output. Full static quality, linked tests, fresh installed npm/Bun SDK and CLI checks, and packed npx/bunx smoke passed."
